    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d898">

                <pb facs="1074" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg1064"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/570: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-05T13:00:00+02:00">April 5, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 5—8:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2395. To Secretary Morgenthau. This morning on returning to the office for the
                    first time I had a telephone call from the Chancellor of the Exchequer to inform
                    me that the White Plan<anchor n="26" xml:id="d898-f1"/> had been published in
                    this morning’s <hi rendition="#italic">Financial News</hi>. The Chancellor told
                    me that the text was in a form which made him believe that it had come from one
                    of the Allied Governments. The Chancellor further explained to me that since I
                    saw you the President had decided to postpone the publication of the White text
                    although the British still planned to publish the Keynes text on
                        Thursday.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d898-f2"/> I understand that the text of the
                    White Plan as published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Financial News</hi> has
                    already in part been cabled to the United States by press correspondents.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d898-f1" n="26" xml:id="d898-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the original White Plan, see <ref target="frus1942v01#pg_178">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 178</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d898-f2" n="27" xml:id="d898-f2-content">
                <p>For text published on April 8, see British Cmd. 6437: <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Proposals for an International Clearing Union;</hi> or <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Proceedings and Documents of the United “Nations
                        Monetary and Financial Conference</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >ii</hi>, p. 1548.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
